WEBVTT

00:04.350 --> 00:04.856
Welcome.

00:04.856 --> 00:07.829
This is a quick tour of your new office system.

00:07.829 --> 00:11.561
In about three minutes, you'll know where everything lives.

00:11.561 --> 00:13.206
You can pause it any time.

00:13.209 --> 00:17.341
This is your dashboard, the first page you see when you sign in.

00:17.341 --> 00:21.474
Across the top are today's numbers: new requests waiting for you

00:21.474 --> 00:24.831
jobs assigned to a technician, and work in progress.

00:24.831 --> 00:28.641
Overdue invoices shows how much money is still owed to you.

00:28.651 --> 00:33.268
Further down, today's schedule lists every job on the books: the customer

00:33.268 --> 00:37.315
what's wrong, the arrival window, and which technician is going.

00:37.318 --> 00:40.708
Every call, text and website chat becomes a request.

00:40.708 --> 00:43.316
Open Requests from the menu on the left.

00:43.316 --> 00:48.206
The newest are at the top, and the colored tags show how urgent each one is

00:48.206 --> 00:49.510
and where it stands.

00:49.512 --> 00:51.890
Click a request to see the details.

00:51.890 --> 00:55.422
Here's the customer's name, phone number and address

00:55.422 --> 00:57.461
and exactly what they told us.

00:57.461 --> 01:02.352
This one is a bakery whose ice machine quit right before the lunch rush.

01:02.362 --> 01:05.806
Further down, the system suggests which technician to send

01:05.806 --> 01:10.319
based on who has done this kind of work before, and how busy they are today.

01:10.319 --> 01:12.754
One click on Assign puts them on the job.

01:12.756 --> 01:15.056
To see the whole day, open the Calendar.

01:15.056 --> 01:18.737
Each technician gets a column, with their jobs laid out by time.

01:18.737 --> 01:22.590
Work that still needs a time waits on the right, under Unscheduled.

01:22.590 --> 01:25.236
Drag it onto a technician's column to book it.

01:26.714 --> 01:30.567
Customers keeps everyone you've worked for in one place.

01:30.567 --> 01:33.251
Search by name, phone, email or address

01:33.251 --> 01:36.554
then open a customer to see their whole history.

01:36.716 --> 01:41.115
Click a customer for a quick look: their phone, email and address

01:41.115 --> 01:45.650
and every request, past and upcoming, with the technician who went.

01:45.650 --> 01:50.252
Open full profile shows their equipment, estimates and invoices too.

01:50.382 --> 01:53.532
Under Money, Estimates is where your quotes live.

01:53.532 --> 01:57.904
The tiles up top show what's still open, what needs a follow-up call

01:57.904 --> 01:59.190
and what you've won.

02:02.737 --> 02:04.980
Invoices is your collections desk.

02:04.980 --> 02:07.817
It shows what's outstanding, what's overdue

02:07.817 --> 02:10.456
and how long each bill has been waiting.

02:10.456 --> 02:11.709
When someone's late

02:11.709 --> 02:16.129
Send reminder sends them a friendly note with a link to pay online.

02:16.665 --> 02:18.009
Next, the Setup guide.

02:18.009 --> 02:22.897
This checklist ticks itself off as you work, so there's nothing to mark by hand.

02:22.897 --> 02:25.647
When a step needs attention, it tells you why

02:25.647 --> 02:29.313
and gives you a button that goes straight to the right page.

02:29.314 --> 02:30.780
Need a refresher later?

02:30.780 --> 02:34.351
Click Quick tour at the bottom of the menu, on any page.

02:34.351 --> 02:38.559
It brings you back here, where you can step through the tour again

02:38.559 --> 02:39.898
or replay this video.

02:41.922 --> 02:44.932
If you ever get stuck, start with the Setup guide.

02:44.932 --> 02:47.400
It always points to the next thing to do.

02:47.400 --> 02:48.363
That's the tour.

02:48.363 --> 02:49.266
Welcome aboard.
